{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792956863,"nonce":"AeRVuGz26syLXjW0Kxc7UfPqv5Y=","title":"Consume browser defaults for editor keyboard shortcuts","message":"The page agent leaves Ctrl/Cmd shortcuts and non-text keys at their browser defaults while IME is enabled. Editor commands can trigger Print, Save, browser navigation or reload as well. Consume application keys synchronously in the focused canvas/textarea handlers, leaving text composition and copy/cut/paste defaults available. Capture printable key text ownership in each queued event rather than reconstructing it from later IME state. Verify Ctrl/Meta shortcuts, F keys, editing keys, clipboard, text entry, composition and browser focus scope.","files":null}]}